   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["Spinor", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Represents a massless helicity spinor, a massive spin spinor, or an \
auxiliary reference spinor.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Spinor", "[", "\"Helicity\"", ",",
         " ", "type", ",", " ", "i", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "represe\
nts a massless external spinor of chirality \"Angle\" or \"Square\"."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Spinor", "[", "\"Spin\"", ",", " ",
         "type", ",", " ", "i", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "represents a massive spinor with its little-group index implicit."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Spinor", "[", "\"Spin\"", ",", " ",
         "variance", ",", " ", "type", ",", " ", "i", ",", " ", "index",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "makes the \"Upper\" or \"Lower\" little-group index explicit."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Spinor", "[", "\"Xi\"", ",", " ",
         "type", ",", " ", "i", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "represents \
an auxiliary reference spinor; its label need not be an external particle."}]\
, "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["Spinors form the endpoints \
of SpinorChain. HEPCAT displays complete chains in angle and square bracket \
notation automatically.", "Notes"], Cell["External particle labels and \
little-group indices have different roles. In the five-argument form, the \
fourth argument labels the particle and the fifth labels its spin index.",
   "Notes"], Cell["HEPCAT uses all external momenta incoming. Use \
ReverseMomentum to cross legs in complete amplitude expressions; changing a \
particle label is not crossing.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
